title: "11d  One foreign project loan: approvals, signing, use of the loan and repayment"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: a project is to be financed by a foreign loan. Which bodies must approve before the loan is signed, and how does the loan money reach the project?
  %% SOURCES: ICC review of every project funded by a foreign loan [ICC-NEWS]. Order of approvals seen in one concessional loan (approval by the NEDA Board, DBM Forward Obligational Authority, Monetary Board approval in principle, Special Presidential Authority, clearance of the Inter-Agency Committee for the Review of Foreign Loan Documents, final Monetary Board approval, legal opinion of DOJ) [ODA]. Documents that DOF sends to the Office of the President and the lead time of 10 working days [MC51]. Prior concurrence of the Monetary Board [CONST VII.20]. Non-Cash Availment Authority for direct payment, MDS sub-account for foreign-assisted projects [NBC599]. Tier 2 profile of foreign-assisted projects, BP Form 203 [NBM156]. BTr services the debt [EO449].
  %% NOTE: the ED Council replaced the NEDA Board in 2025 [AO37]. The loan in the source was approved before that change.
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: step 3 (request to provide for the project in the budget), step 13 (declaration of effectiveness), steps 14, 15 and 17 (withdrawal application, direct payment, proceeds to the Treasury), the rule that the project still needs an appropriation in the GAA.
  participant AGY as Implementing<br/>agency
  participant DEP as DEPDev, ICC,<br/>ED Council
  participant DBM as DBM
  participant DOF as DOF
  participant MB as Monetary Board<br/>(BSP)
  participant OP as Office of the<br/>President
  participant LEN as Lender
  participant DOJ as DOJ
  participant BTR as BTr

  Note over AGY,OP: BEFORE SIGNING
  AGY->>DEP: Project proposal for ICC review
  DEP-->>AGY: ICC recommendation, ED Council approval
  AGY->>DBM: Request to provide for the project in the budget
  DBM-->>DOF: Forward Obligational Authority (project loan)
  DOF->>MB: Request for approval in principle of the loan terms
  MB-->>DOF: Approval in principle
  DOF->>OP: Request for Special Authority, at least 10 working days before the date needed, with:<br/>agency letter, draft loan agreement, Monetary Board concurrence,<br/>statement of compliance with laws, Forward Obligational Authority
  OP-->>DOF: Special Authority (or Full Powers) to negotiate and sign

  Note over DOF,DOJ: SIGNING
  DOF->>LEN: Negotiation. Loan documents cleared by the<br/>inter-agency committee that reviews foreign loan documents
  DOF->>LEN: Loan agreement signed
  MB-->>DOF: Final approval of the loan terms
  DOJ-->>DOF: Legal opinion on the authority of the borrower
  LEN-->>DOF: Loan declared effective

  Note over AGY,BTR: USE OF THE LOAN. The project also needs an appropriation and an allotment like any other spending.
  alt Direct payment
    AGY->>LEN: Withdrawal application for a supplier's bill
    LEN->>LEN: Pays the supplier directly<br/>#nbsp;
    DBM-->>AGY: Non-Cash Availment Authority, so that the<br/>payment is recorded in the books
  else Cash through the Treasury
    LEN->>BTR: Loan proceeds to the Treasury
    DBM-->>AGY: NCA under the MDS sub-account for foreign-assisted projects
  end

  Note over DOF,BTR: REPAYMENT
  BTR->>LEN: Interest and principal on the due dates,<br/>from the Treasury Single Account
